  "question": {
    "text": "The rate of growth of bacteria in a culture is proportional to the number of bacteria present and the bacteria count is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn></math> at initial time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The number of bacteria is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> hours. If the population of bacteria is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2000</mn></math> after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math> hours, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>k</mi><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to:",
